.IX Title "File::Rename::Options 3pm"
.TH File::Rename::Options 3pm "2023-01-23" "perl v5.36.0" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
File::Rename::Options \- Option processing for File::Rename
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 3
\&    use File::Rename::Options;
\&    my $options = File::Rename::Options::GetOptions()
\&        or pod2usage;
\&
\&    use File::Rename::Options qw(no_require_order);
.Ve
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
.SS "\s-1CONFIGUATION\s0"
.IX Subsection "CONFIGUATION"
The parameters to \f(CW\*(C`use File::Rename::Options\*(C'\fR are 
configurations settings for Getopt::Long
.PP
The default configuration is posix_default and no_ignore_case;
other settings are added to this list.
.SS "\s-1FUNCTIONS\s0"
.IX Subsection "FUNCTIONS"
.ie n .IP """GetOptions()""" 4
.el .IP "\f(CWGetOptions()\fR" 4
.IX Item "GetOptions()"
Call \f(CW\*(C`Getopt::Long::GetOptions()\*(C'\fR with options for rename script,
returning a \s-1HASH\s0 of options.
.ie n .IP """bad_encoding($options)""" 4
.el .IP "\f(CWbad_encoding($options)\fR" 4
.IX Item "bad_encoding($options)"
Test if \fIencoding\fR does not look like an encoding
.SS "\s-1OPTIONS\s0"
.IX Subsection "OPTIONS"
See rename script for options (in \f(CW@ARGV\fR).
.PP
See File::Rename for structure of the options \s-1HASH\s0
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
No environment variables are used.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBFile::Rename\fR\|(3), \fBrename\fR\|(1)
.SH "AUTHOR"
.IX Header "AUTHOR"
Robin Barker <RMBarker@cpan.org>
.SH "DIAGNOSTICS"
.IX Header "DIAGNOSTICS"
Returns \f(CW\*(C`undef\*(C'\fR when there is an error in the options.
